
Every new version or os, lots of lovely new problems. Guillaume
incorporated lots of dependencies on boost. While this provides
great syntax, the mavericks upgrade screwed things up. 

Macports installed boost seems to have problems. To fix.

Use clang++.
Use homebrew boost
Make sure the numeric-bindings are in include from the git trunk
Make sure numeric/bindings/ is in the include.


15th Sept 2020
The boost bindings officially failed with macOS catalina.
they probably failed with mojave also but I didn't notice.
To fix: we have removed them. I have written an expm_real function
that uses LAPACKE bindings directly to LAPACK, avoiding the 
need to call LAPACK from boost.
17th Sept 2020
Re-written again to use lapack directly, manually declaring the 
work spaces. This gets a factor of 9 in speed versus expm_pad.
All instances of expm_pad have been removed.


#using expm_pad: seriously slow.
#using deltaR2 calc on Reid's data: 2.25 using boos::ublas::expm
#using a lapack eigenvalue expm_eig, 46s
#using the expokit dgpadm, 39s.
#one problem: I need to declare the memory for Gfree in the matrix
#exponential functions. which seems bad. Doing test calculations,
#the ratio should be roughly 60:5:1 for speed (pade boost,eig,pade expokit)

#last improvement: replaced prod from ublas in boost with dgemm 
#coming directly from blas. the improvement is absolutely huge.
#using expokit dgpadm we are down to just 7 seconds. 

#we have sped catia up by a factor of 124. That is immense. 


26th March 2024
